00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:44.640
amazing things they are working for&nbsp;
nasa they are designing robots they are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:53.200
winning the world poker tournaments and and I&nbsp;
just thought it would be funny if one of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.200 --> 00:01:00.480
spelling bee winners grew up to be unsuccessful&nbsp;
a loser living in their mom's basement playing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:06.720
video games just not doing much with her life&nbsp;
so that was that was the gist of my sketch and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:15.680
this was four pages long and then I in at the end&nbsp;
of 2016 I got into a Sundance screenwriting lab&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:22.480
and I went to the screenwriting lab and it&nbsp;
was really inspiring and amazing and in 2017&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:27.680
a couple months later I decided to go to the&nbsp;
Sundance film festival for the first time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:34.400
and I went as a Sundance influencer Sundance asked&nbsp;
me to take over their instagram and their twitter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:39.680
and go to certain events and interview people&nbsp;
and it was actually a great way to experience a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:46.000
first Sundance kind of within the Sundance&nbsp;
family and my friend Justin Chon's film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:54.400
was playing there and so I went to the premiere&nbsp;
and was just completely blown away by the film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.400 --> 00:02:00.720
and I cornered him at his post party and&nbsp;
I asked him how he got it made and he said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:07.120
